              <animate attributeName="r" values="9;12;9" dur="1.6s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
            </circle>
          </svg>

          <div class="gen-detail" id="gen-detail">
            <span class="gen-detail-arch">RDNA3 (gfx1100)</span>
            <span class="gen-detail-text">First gen with the WMMA matrix unit. 16&times;16 fp16 tile per issue, ~123 TFLOPs theoretical. A historical prefill snapshot discussed below reported 2.94&times; for its cross-arch fixture.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>arch</th>
              <th>LLVM target</th>
              <th class="num">wave</th>
              <th class="num">VGPRs / SIMD</th>
              <th class="num">waves / SIMD</th>
              <th class="num">LDS / CU</th>
              <th>matrix path</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Navi 10 (5700 XT)</td><td><code>gfx1010</code></td><td class="num">32</td><td class="num">1024</td><td class="num">20</td><td class="num">64 KB</td><td><strong>dp4a only</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Navi 21 (6900 XT)</td><td><code>gfx1030</code></td><td class="num">32</td><td class="num">1024</td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">64 KB</td><td><strong>dp4a only</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Navi 31 (7900 XT/XTX)</td><td><code>gfx1100</code></td><td class="num">32</td><td class="num">1024</td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">64 KB</td><td class="accent"><strong>WMMA</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Navi 32 / 33</td><td><code>gfx1101</code> / <code>gfx1102</code></td><td class="num">32</td><td class="num">1024</td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">64 KB</td><td class="accent"><strong>WMMA</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Strix Halo APU</td><td><code>gfx1150</code> / <code>gfx1151</code></td><td class="num">32</td><td class="num">1024</td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">64 KB</td><td class="accent"><strong>WMMA</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Navi 48 / 44 (RX 9070)</td><td><code>gfx1200</code> / <code>gfx1201</code></td><td class="num">32</td><td class="num">1536</td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">128 KB</td><td class="accent"><strong>WMMA32</strong></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>Two structural breaks worth memorizing:</p>
      <ol class="distil-ol">
        <li>
          <strong>RDNA1/2 &rarr; RDNA3</strong> is where the matrix unit
          appears. Before <code>gfx1100</code>, the fastest f16-mac path is
          <code>v_dot2_f32_f16</code> (a 2-wide packed-FMA) or
          <code>v_dot4_i32_i8</code> (dp4a). After <code>gfx1100</code>, you
          have <code>v_wmma_*</code> with a 16&times;16 accumulator per wave.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>RDNA3 &rarr; RDNA4</strong> keeps the wave32 / WMMA shape but
          widens it: 1.5&times; the VGPR file per SIMD, 2&times; the LDS per
          CU, and a 32-element WMMA tile (<code>WMMA32</code>). Most kernels
          need their own <code>.gfx12.hip</code> variant to get the speedup.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================ 2 -->
    <section class="distil-section">
      <h2><span class="num">02</span> CDNA vs RDNA &mdash; the divergence summary</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th></th>
              <th><strong>CDNA &mdash; Instinct</strong><br/><span class="cell-sub">MFMA path, data center</span></th>
              <th><strong>RDNA &mdash; Radeon / Ryzen AI</strong><br/><span class="cell-sub">WMMA path, consumer</span></th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Wavefront</td><td><strong>64 threads</strong></td><td><strong>32 threads</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Matrix unit</td><td><strong>MFMA</strong> (<code>v_mfma_*</code>) &mdash; 16&times;16&times;16 fp16, 32&times;32&times;8 bf16, FP8 on CDNA 3</td><td><strong>WMMA</strong> (<code>v_wmma_*</code>) &mdash; 16&times;16&times;16 fp16 (RDNA3) / WMMA32 (RDNA4)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Memory</td><td>HBM3 / HBM3E / HBM4 (192&ndash;288 GB)</td><td>GDDR6 / GDDR6X (8&ndash;24 GB) or shared system RAM (Strix Halo)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cache</td><td>Large L2, compute-optimized</td><td>Smaller L1/L2 + <strong>Infinity Cache</strong> (256 MB+ on dGPU)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Graphics</td><td class="warn">None (no rasterizer, no RT, no display)</td><td class="ok">Full graphics + RT pipeline</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Transistor budget</td><td>More CUs, bigger matrix engines, more HBM controllers</td><td>Display engines, rasterizer, RT cores compete with compute</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Typical port</td><td><code>gfx908 / gfx90a / gfx942 / gfx950</code></td><td><code>gfx1010 &rarr; gfx1201</code></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        <strong>Why this matters for code:</strong> the same <code>.hip</code>
        file compiles for either family &mdash; but a CDNA kernel ported to
        RDNA hits three landmines: wavefront width (64 &rarr; 32 halves the
        lanes seen by <code>__shfl_*</code>), matrix intrinsic (<code>v_mfma_*</code>
        doesn't exist on RDNA &mdash; you must call <code>v_wmma_*</code>),
        and memory-tier sizing (256 MB Infinity Cache changes your tiling
        math vs HBM-direct).
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================ 3 -->
    <section class="distil-section">
      <h2><span class="num">03</span> WMMA &mdash; one instruction, one 16&times;16 tile</h2>
      <p>
        The WMMA family is RDNA3+'s answer to CDNA's MFMA. Same shape &mdash;
        a fused <code>D = A &times; B + C</code> over a 16&times;16 tile
        &mdash; but reachable from wave32 (half the lanes) and from a
        fundamentally consumer-silicon caches.
      </p>
      <p>The canonical RDNA3 builtin (used in hipfire's <code>gemm_f16_wmma.hip</code>):</p>
      <pre class="prose-pre"><code>{`// WMMA layout: __builtin_amdgcn_wmma_f32_16x16x16_f16_w32(a, b, c)
// computes  D[i][j] = sum_k a[i][k] * b[j][k] + c[i][j]
// which is  D = A @ B^T + C.
//
// A is half16_t (16 fp16 values per lane)
// B is half16_t
// C / D are float8_t (8 fp32 accumulators per lane on wave32)

typedef _Float16 __attribute__((ext_vector_type(16))) half16_t;
typedef float    __attribute__((ext_vector_type(8)))  float8_t;

__launch_bounds__(32, 2)
extern "C" __global__ void gemm_f16_wmma(
    const _Float16* __restrict__ W, const float* __restrict__ X,
    float*          __restrict__ Y, int M, int K, int N)
{
    // Grid: [ceil(M/16), ceil(N/16)],  Block: [32]
    float8_t acc = {0.f, 0.f, 0.f, 0.f, 0.f, 0.f, 0.f, 0.f};
    for (int k0 = 0; k0 < K; k0 += 16) {
        half16_t a_reg, b_reg;
        // ...load 16x16 tiles into a_reg and b_reg...
        acc = __builtin_amdgcn_wmma_f32_16x16x16_f16_w32(a_reg, b_reg, acc);
    }
    // ...store acc back to Y...
}`}</code></pre>

      <div class="distil-fig" data-widget="wmma">
        <div class="fig-caption">interactive &middot; v_wmma_f32_NxNxN_f16 &middot; one issue, one tile</div>
        <div class="mfma-body">
          <div class="mfma-eq">
            <div class="mfma-tile" data-tile="A">
              <div class="mfma-tile-grid" id="wmma-A"></div>
              <div class="mfma-tile-label">A &middot; <span class="mfma-dtype">fp16</span> &middot; <span class="wmma-dim-label">16&times;16</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mfma-op">&times;</div>
            <div class="mfma-tile" data-tile="B">
              <div class="mfma-tile-grid" id="wmma-B"></div>
              <div class="mfma-tile-label">B &middot; <span class="mfma-dtype">fp16</span> &middot; <span class="wmma-dim-label">16&times;16</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mfma-op">+</div>
            <div class="mfma-tile" data-tile="C">
              <div class="mfma-tile-grid" id="wmma-C"></div>
              <div class="mfma-tile-label">C &middot; <span class="mfma-dtype">fp32</span> &middot; accumulator</div>
            </div>
            <div class="mfma-op">=</div>
            <div class="mfma-tile" data-tile="D">
              <div class="mfma-tile-grid" id="wmma-D"></div>
              <div class="mfma-tile-label">D &middot; <span class="mfma-dtype">fp32</span> &middot; result</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="wmma-lanes">
            <span class="wmma-lanes-label">wave32 lanes contributing:</span>
            <div class="wmma-lane-strip" id="wmma-lane-strip"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="wmma-k-progress" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="wmma-k-label">K-loop iteration</span>
            <div class="wmma-k-strip" id="wmma-k-strip"></div>
            <span class="wmma-k-counter" id="wmma-k-counter">0 / 16</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mfma-issue">
            <span class="mfma-issue-counter" id="wmma-issue-counter">1</span>
            issue &middot; <span class="mfma-issue-label" id="wmma-label">256 fma per issue &mdash; ~123 TFLOPs on 7900 XTX</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mfma-variants">
            <button class="mfma-variant active" data-variant="wmma_f16_16">RDNA3 &middot; 16&times;16&times;16 fp16</button>
            <button class="mfma-variant" data-variant="wmma_bf16_16">RDNA3 &middot; bf16</button>
            <button class="mfma-variant" data-variant="wmma_i8_16">RDNA3 &middot; i8 (dp4a-on-WMMA)</button>
            <button class="mfma-variant" data-variant="wmma32">RDNA4 &middot; WMMA32</button>
          </div>

          <dl class="wmma-info" id="wmma-info">
            <div class="wmma-info-row">
              <dt>tile shape</dt>
              <dd id="wmma-info-tile">M=16, N=16, K=16</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="wmma-info-row">
              <dt>inputs &middot; output</dt>
              <dd id="wmma-info-dtype">fp16 &times; fp16 &rarr; fp32 accumulator</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="wmma-info-row">
              <dt>per issue</dt>
              <dd id="wmma-info-ops">256 fma ops &middot; 16-element dot product per output cell</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="wmma-info-row">
              <dt>theoretical peak</dt>
              <dd id="wmma-info-peak">~123 TFLOPs &middot; 7900 XTX (gfx1100)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="wmma-info-row">
              <dt>notes</dt>
              <dd id="wmma-info-notes">Training-class precision. Default WMMA path on RDNA3.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>What WMMA gives you (RDNA3, gfx1100 / 1151):</h3>
      <ul class="distil-ul">
        <li>
          One <code>v_wmma_f32_16x16x16_f16</code> issue per CU per cycle
          group; ~256 fp16 MACs per cycle per CU = the headline TFLOPs
          (e.g. 7900 XTX &asymp; 123 TFLOPs fp16 WMMA, vs &asymp; 41 TFLOPs
          from packed dot2).
        </li>
        <li>
          Wave32 native &mdash; <code>_w32</code> suffix on the builtin. The
          wave64 sibling exists for CDNA-style code paths but RDNA3 issues
          wave32.
        </li>
        <li>
          The accumulator (<code>float8_t</code> on wave32,
          <code>float16_t</code> on wave64) lives in the VGPR file, so a
          fused-GEMM kernel typically lands at <strong>80&ndash;120
          VGPRs/wave</strong> even without spills &mdash; see &sect; 06 for
          what that does to occupancy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What WMMA32 (RDNA4, gfx1200+) adds:</h3>
      <ul class="distil-ul">
        <li>
          32-element matrix tiles (the <code>WMMA32</code> family) &mdash;
          bigger tile, same wave32 shape. Most existing 16-tile kernels need
          their own <code>.gfx12.hip</code> override to switch to the wider
          builtin.
        </li>
        <li>
          1.5&times; the register file (1536 VGPRs/SIMD) means the bigger
          accumulator footprint doesn't cost occupancy proportionally.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================ 4 -->
    <section class="distil-section">
      <h2><span class="num">04</span> The roofline &mdash; three matrix paths, one chip</h2>
      <p>
        Because RDNA3 ships both <code>v_wmma_*</code> and
        <code>v_dot2_f32_f16</code> (and the scalar fallback), it has
        <strong>three different compute ceilings</strong> on the same chip.
        Which one bounds you is decided by your kernel's matrix path, not by
        the GPU's nameplate TFLOPs.
      </p>

      <div class="distil-fig" data-widget="roofline">
        <div class="fig-caption">interactive &middot; roofline &middot; 7900 XTX &middot; drag the batch-size slider</div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 640 320" class="roofline-svg" role="img" aria-label="Roofline plot with movable workload">
          <!-- bound regime shading (toggled by JS) -->
          <rect id="rl-shade-mem"     x="60"  y="30"  width="160" height="250" class="rl-shade rl-shade-mem"     opacity="0.18"/>
          <rect id="rl-shade-dot2"    x="220" y="180" width="220" height="100" class="rl-shade rl-shade-dot2"    opacity="0"/>
